-- An accident on 1 March 2026, discharged on 10 March: the file is due by 6 September 2026.
-- A disablement that began on 5 March and is not in the table meets definition 18 only on
-- 2 March 2028 (104 weeks on). The file is due 18 months before the claim can exist.
`a ten-day stay after the accident` MEANS
    `an event: cause` `an accident` `, accident` (JUST `the standard accident`) `, illness` NOTHING `, diagnoses` EMPTY `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` (JUST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, hours` 216 `, admitted` TRUE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a hospital in Vietnam`))

`the accident claim discharged on 10 March` MEANS
    `a claim by` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for` `a ten-day stay after the accident` `with the lines` EMPTY

#ASSERT `the last day to submit the claim file for` `the accident claim discharged on 10 March` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 6
#ASSERT `the last day to submit the claim file for` `the accident claim discharged on 10 March` LESS THAN ((YMD 2026 3 5) PLUS 728)

§§ `X26 — A death claim has no day from which its time limits run`
-- src:650 | thường của PTI trong vòng 180 ngày kể từ ngày điều trị cuối cùng. Đối với trường hợp nằm viện, ngày điều trị cuối cùng là ngày
-- src:651 | ra viện. Đối với trường hợp điều trị ngoại trú, ngày điều trị cuối cùng là ngày có kết quả chẩn đoán bệnh.
-- A death from an accident with no hospital stay and no outpatient treatment: Part 5 clause 1
-- fixes the day of last treatment for neither, so whether the claim is late cannot be said,
-- and the whole claim cannot be assessed.
`a death with no treatment` MEANS
    `The event` WITH `the cause` IS `an accident`, `the accident` IS JUST `the standard accident`, `the illness` IS NOTHING, `the conditions diagnosed` IS EMPTY, `the circumstances` IS EMPTY, `the sporting activity` IS NOTHING, `the hospital stay` IS NOTHING, `the date of death` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 2), `the cause of death unknown` IS FALSE, `the disablement` IS NOTHING, `the date the surgery was first ordered` IS NOTHING, `the date of the outpatient diagnosis` IS NOTHING

`the death line` MEANS `a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 2)

`a death claim` MEANS
    `a claim by` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for` `a death with no treatment` `with the lines` (LIST `the death line`)

#ASSERT REFUSED `the total payable on the claim` `a death claim` BECAUSE "Part 5 clause 1 fixes the day of last treatment only for a hospital stay and for outpatient treatment"

